As you may see from my earlier posting.  I had the same trouble.  You
have to have some way to connect to the port it's listening on.  You
run the server in the background and redirect stdout and stderr to a
file or /dev/null.  The use something telnet or write something in
emacs to send and listen to the server.  I started the server on
the machine 'watnow', so to connect I used:

telnet watnow 4201

This works.  Better ideas would still be appreciated.

